<title>UK: DEUTSCHE BANK SETS DOLLAR/MARK CURRENCY WARRANTS.</title>
<headline>DEUTSCHE BANK SETS DOLLAR/MARK CURRENCY WARRANTS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deutsche Bank AG, Frankfurt said it has issued</p>
<p>two million European-style call with cap warrants, in two equal tranches, the</p>
<p>U.S. dollar/mark exchange rate.</p>
<p>COMMON TERMS:</p>
<p> EXPIRATION	16.MAR.98		 PAYDATE   14.AUG.97</p>
<p> LISTING	   FFURT, DUSS	     SPOT REF  $/DEM 1.8876</p>
<p>* * * * * *</p>
<p> TYPE		STRIKE    CAP	  ISSUE</p>
<p> CALL WITH CAP   1.75 DEM  1.85 DEM   13.35 DEM</p>
<p> CALL WITH CAP   1.85 DEM  1.95 DEM    7.14 DEM</p>
<p>--Reuter London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
